<div class="faq-item"><h3>What makes Clementine Design Studio the best Squarespace designer for small businesses?</h3><p>I believe the best Squarespace designer is one who balances aesthetics with autonomy. At Clementine Design Studio, I don't just build functional, professional websites; I empower you to own them. I don’t believe any business should be “held hostage” by a designer to make simple tweaks and edits to their website. </p><p>Unlike developers who code from scratch (making future edits difficult), I specialize in Squarespace because it allows my clients to easily update their sites without any website knowledge. I combine high-end design with US-based expertise to help you get new clients and establish your brand.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>I’m on a tight budget. Do you offer affordable Squarespace design packages?</h3><p>Yes. I understand that small businesses often need high-quality design on a timeline. I offer a specific "Website-in-a-Day" package ($1,500 for 1 to 5 pages) designed for those strapped for time or budget. This ensures you get a professional launch without the wait. For clients seeking a more deeply collaborative process, I also provide my Custom Website package (from $3,000 for 5+ pages).</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Do you offer SEO services to help my Squarespace site rank on Google?</h3><p>Absolutely. A beautiful website is only effective if your ideal clients can find it. I go beyond design by performing SEO audits and providing strategic advice on how to rank higher on Google. My goal is to ensure your site is optimized to get the most eyes on your content, driving sales and engagement from day one.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Can I hire you for small updates if I already have a Squarespace website?</h3><p>Yes, I offer hourly Squarespace help. If you have an existing site that needs professional polish, tweaks, or specific improvements to meet your standards, you can book me at $150 an hour. This is perfect for business owners who need expert assistance without committing to a full redesign.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Will I know how to use my website after you finish designing it?</h3><p>Empowering my clients is a core part of my process. At the end of every website build, I provide an optional lesson to teach you how to make changes on your own. Because most of the sites I build are on Squarespace, you won't need to learn code to swap out images or update text, ensuring your site grows with your business.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Are you a US-based Squarespace designer?</h3><p>Yes, I’m an experienced Squarespace designer based in the US. I pride myself on clear communication and a personal touch. When you work with me, you’re working directly with the person who takes the time to understand your unique vision, rather than having your project outsourced overseas.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>How much does a professional Squarespace website design cost?</h3><p>Most professional custom Squarespace websites range from $2,500 to $8,000+, depending on complexity and number of pages. At Clementine Design Studio, a Website-in-a-Day is $1,500 for 1 to 5 pages, and a Custom Website starts at $3,000 for 5+ pages, ensuring you get a fully optimized, custom site without hidden agency fees.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>How long does it take to design a custom Squarespace website?</h3><p>A custom Squarespace website typically takes about 3 to 4 weeks from start to launch. This timeline includes the strategy phase, design mockups, development, and SEO setup. For clients on a tight deadline, I also offer Website-in-a-Day, where your site is up in one day.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Do you offer payment plans for website design?</h3><p>Yes, I split the project investment into manageable payments. Typically, this is a 50% deposit to book your slot, and the remaining 50% due upon project completion and launch. We can also discuss custom payment schedules for larger projects.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Why should I hire a Squarespace Expert instead of doing it myself (DIY)?</h3><p>While Squarespace is user-friendly, a Squarespace Expert (like Clementine Design Studio) brings advanced knowledge of CSS coding, SEO strategy, and conversion design that templates cannot provide. I don't just make it look good; I build it to rank on Google and convert visitors into clients, saving you hundreds of frustrating hours.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Do you have a degree in web design?</h3><p>Yes, unlike many self-taught designers, I hold a BA degree in Web Design and have over 7 years of commercial experience. This academic background ensures your site is built on solid design principles, accessibility standards, and technical reliability.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Can you help my website rank higher on Google (SEO)?</h3><p>Absolutely. I don't just design; I build for search engines. Every Custom Website includes SEO setup: keyword-optimized headings, meta descriptions, image alt text, and a clean URL structure to help you rank for terms like "best squarespace designer" or local services in your niche. With a Website-in-a-Day, you can add SEO later.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Is Squarespace a good platform for therapists and private practices?</h3><p>Yes, Squarespace is the #1 recommended platform for therapists because of its security, and ease of use. I can seamlessly integrate booking tools like SimplePractice, Jane App, or Calendly so clients can schedule appointments directly from your site.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Can you migrate my current site from WordPress or Wix to Squarespace?</h3><p>Yes, I specialize in platform migrations. I will safely transfer your domain, site content, and blog posts from WordPress, Wix, or Showit over to Squarespace, ensuring you don't lose your hard-earned traffic or SEO rankings during the move.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Will I be able to update the website myself after you finish?</h3><p>Yes! One of the main reasons I use Squarespace is its client-friendly interface. Upon launch, I provide a recorded 1-on-1 training session teaching you how to edit text, swap photos, and publish blog posts, empowering you to own your website without paying for monthly maintenance.</p></div>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Do you use custom code (CSS) or just standard templates?</h3><p>I only create fully custom designs. While I start with the robust Squarespace framework, I use custom CSS and HTML to break the "template mold," giving you a unique look that matches your brand perfectly while keeping the site easy for you to manage.</p></div>
